{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target platform is Spring Framework 6.x running on Java 17+, built on top of the existing XD-style runtime (stream DSL, source/sink module model, singlenode and distributed containers, pluggable message bus).",
    "U1 (mass ingestion) is implemented as launchable batch job modules rather than streams: a 'jdbc-to-hdfs' job that extracts a table/query via JDBC (paged ItemReader) and writes delimited-text or Avro files to HDFS using the Hadoop FileSystem API with chunked, parallel writes for efficiency, plus HAWQ/GPDB loading implemented via the gpfdist external-table protocol (HTTP-based data server that GPDB segments read in parallel).",
    "Existing open-source components are reused where possible (Spring Batch for job orchestration, Hadoop client libraries, an existing gpfdist protocol implementation) instead of writing everything from scratch.",
    "U2 is executed as a time-boxed spike only: study the Kafka simple (low-level) consumer API (explicit partition assignment, manual offset management, leader failover handling), build a throwaway prototype, and produce a findings document with recommended approach and next steps; no production module is delivered for U2.",
    "U3 is implemented as a new admin REST endpoint (POST /modules, multipart/form-data uber-jar upload) with jar validation (module metadata, size limit, duplicate/version handling), persistence to a shared module repository, and distribution to all containers via ZooKeeper watch events; containers load uploaded modules in isolated classloaders with runtime registry refresh. Existing admin basic authentication is reused; no UI is built.",
    "U5 generator source exposes options numMsgs (default 10000), msgSize (default 1024) and numThreads (default 1); it generates deterministic fixed-size payloads, uses a shared atomic counter across producer threads, sends through the configured message-bus binder with backpressure, and stops cleanly after numMsgs messages.",
    "U6 perf-meter sink exposes option numMsgs (default 1000); it writes a log line (timestamp, cumulative message count, message rate since the previous log event) to the standard container log via SLF4J/Logback every numMsgs messages.",
    "U7 performance measurement runs 'generator | perf-meter' on a singlenode container with 1,000,000 messages of 1000 bytes on one thread; the baseline is measured with the default local singlenode transport and repeated with the Kafka bus provisioned from the U4 sample project for comparison.",
    "U8 test coverage uses JUnit 5 with mocked Kafka clients for unit tests and an embedded Kafka broker (spring-kafka-test / EmbeddedKafkaBroker) for integration tests, wired into the existing CI pipeline as part of the standard build.",
    "U4 is delivered as a standalone GitHub project containing Docker Compose provisioning (ZooKeeper, Kafka, XD admin and containers), topic-creation scripts, configuration for Kafka as message bus and Kafka as source, sample stream definitions, and a step-by-step README.",
    "Build is a Maven multi-module build; deployable modules are packaged as uber-jars carrying module metadata consumed by the XD module registry and the new upload endpoint."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "An existing XD-style runtime already provides the stream DSL, singlenode/distributed containers, module packaging model, a working Kafka message-bus implementation, and existing Kafka source and sink modules; this increment extends that codebase rather than building it from scratch (U8 and U4 both presuppose existing Kafka modules).",
    "U1 scope is limited to relational databases reachable via JDBC (single table or ad-hoc query extract) into HDFS (delimited text or Avro) and loading into HAWQ/GPDB via gpfdist; 'and others' source types are out of scope for this increment.",
    "The Hadoop/HDFS test environment has no Kerberos or TLS; security integration for Hadoop is out of scope.",
    "U2 delivers only the spike outputs (study, prototype, findings document with approach and next steps); implementing a simple-consumer-based production Kafka source is a future increment.",
    "For U3 there is a single admin server, containers register via ZooKeeper, uber-jars are limited to 100 MB, re-upload of an existing module version is idempotent/rejected with a clear error, and no rolling-upgrade, HA-failover or UI work is included.",
    "Test infrastructure is available: Docker-based Kafka/ZooKeeper locally, hadoop-minicluster for HDFS tests, PostgreSQL/HSQLDB for JDBC tests, a gpfdist protocol mock for automated GPDB/HAWQ tests, and a shared GPDB/HAWQ appliance for occasional manual verification.",
    "An existing CI server (e.g., Jenkins/GitHub Actions) is available; only pipeline configuration is needed.",
    "All work is performed by one developer (myself); figures are work-hours of effort, not elapsed calendar duration.",
    "Unit testing is included within each development activity; integration testing, performance runs, end-to-end verification and documentation are separate activities.",
    "Documentation scope is limited to module reference docs, REST API documentation, the spike findings document, the performance report, and the sample project README."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "1.1",
      "activity_name": "Project setup, build and CI pipeline configuration",
      "activity_description": "Set up the development environment (Java 17, Spring 6 baseline), Maven multi-module structure, local Docker-based Kafka/ZooKeeper tooling, and configure the CI pipeline skeleton used later by U8.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.2",
      "activity_name": "Solution architecture and detailed design",
      "activity_description": "Define module contracts and option metadata for the new modules, design the JDBC-to-HDFS and gpfdist ingestion flow, design the module upload REST API and ZooKeeper distribution model, and record key decisions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.1",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement JDBC-to-HDFS ingestion job module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the batch job that extracts a table/query via JDBC (paged reader), maps rows to delimited text or Avro, and writes to HDFS with chunked/parallel writes; includes job parameters (connection, query, target directory, format, delimiter), basic restartability and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 60
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement HAWQ/GPDB load support via gpfdist",
      "activity_description": "Implement the gpfdist-protocol data server module and load job so HAWQ/GPDB segments can pull extracted data in parallel through external tables; reuses an existing gpfdist implementation where possible; includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.3",
      "activity_name": "U1: Ingestion integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Automated integration tests for the ingestion path using hadoop-minicluster, a test database (PostgreSQL/HSQLDB) and a gpfdist protocol mock, verifying end-to-end extract, write and load behaviour.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.1",
      "activity_name": "U2: Kafka simple consumer API spike",
      "activity_description": "Time-boxed spike: study the simple (low-level) consumer API for explicit partition assignment, deterministic offset management and leader failover; build a throwaway prototype; document findings, recommended approach and next steps.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.1",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement module upload REST endpoint",
      "activity_description": "Implement POST /modules on the admin server accepting a multipart uber-jar: validation of module metadata and jar structure, size limits, duplicate/version handling, persistence to the module repository, error handling and API documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.2",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement module distribution to containers",
      "activity_description": "Implement cluster distribution of uploaded modules via ZooKeeper watch events: container listeners, jar propagation to container module directories, runtime module registry refresh and isolated classloader loading, including handling of containers joining after upload.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.3",
      "activity_name": "U3: Tests for module upload and distribution",
      "activity_description": "REST-level tests (upload, validation failures, duplicates) and integration tests verifying that an uploaded custom module becomes deployable and usable in a stream on containers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.1",
      "activity_name": "U4: Sample GitHub project for provisioning XD with Kafka",
      "activity_description": "Create the reference GitHub project: Docker Compose provisioning for ZooKeeper, Kafka, XD admin and containers; configuration for Kafka as message bus and Kafka as source; topic creation scripts; sample stream definitions; step-by-step README; verification of the provisioning flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.1",
      "activity_name": "U5: Implement generator source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the generator source with options numMsgs (default 10000), msgSize (default 1024) and numThreads (default 1): deterministic fixed-size payload generation, multi-threaded production with shared atomic counter, binder send with backpressure, clean completion, packaging and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.2",
      "activity_name": "U6: Implement perf-meter sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the perf-meter sink with option numMsgs (default 1000): message counting, timestamp capture, rate-since-last-log-event calculation, SLF4J output to the container log in the specified format, packaging and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.1",
      "activity_name": "U7: Performance environment setup and test plan",
      "activity_description": "Provision the singlenode container environment for performance testing and define the test plan (1M messages, 1000-byte payloads, single thread, metrics to capture, repeat runs).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.2",
      "activity_name": "U7: Execute performance runs and document characteristics",
      "activity_description": "Deploy 'generator | perf-meter', run the 1M-message tests (baseline on local transport, plus a Kafka-bus comparison using the U4 topology), collect throughput/latency/resource metrics, analyse results and write the performance characteristics report.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.1",
      "activity_name": "U8: Unit tests for Kafka source and sink modules",
      "activity_description": "Write JUnit 5 unit tests for the existing Kafka source and sink modules covering record mapping, serializer/deserializer configuration, partitioning, offset commit behaviour and error paths using mocked Kafka clients.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.2",
      "activity_name": "U8: Embedded-Kafka integration tests and CI wiring",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests that deploy streams using the Kafka source and sink against an embedded Kafka broker (round-trip, failure/restart scenarios) and wire all module tests into the CI build so they run as part of standard CI builds.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.1",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end verification and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Cross-feature end-to-end verification of the complete increment (ingestion jobs, module upload and distribution, generator/perf-meter streams, sample project flow) on singlenode and container deployments, including fixing defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.2",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release packaging",
      "activity_description": "Write module reference documentation (generator, perf-meter, ingestion jobs), REST API documentation for module upload, finalise the U2 findings document and U7 performance report, update READMEs, and prepare release artifacts and release notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 508
  }
}

